WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:05.928
Think of the outline as a box that cannot stretch; every block has to fit inside.

2
00:00:07.018 --> 00:00:12.786
Move E to the right; starting at nine with width two puts its right edge at eleven.

3
00:00:13.876 --> 00:00:19.908
The outline ends at ten, so the layout fails even though most of E remains inside.

4
00:00:20.998 --> 00:00:28.110
Return E to seven, touching C; their shared boundary has no area and is not an overlap.

5
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:35.136
If E moves one more unit left, will its interior share positive area with C?

6
00:00:36.876 --> 00:00:43.436
Now watch the move; the blocks share a region with positive width, so the layout needs repair.

7
00:00:44.526 --> 00:00:51.470
Finally, check the names; five rectangles do not necessarily mean the five required blocks.

8
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:59.240
In the lab, create overflow and overlap yourself, then use the checker’s reasons to repair them.
